--- !u!114 &1032769213
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 1032769211}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: f4688fdb7df04437aeb418b961361dc5, type: 3}
  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  m_Material: {fileID: 0}
  m_Color: {r: 1, g: 1, b: 1, a: 1}
  m_RaycastTarget: 1
  m_RaycastPadding: {x: 0, y: 0, z: 0, w: 0}
  m_Maskable: 1
  m_OnCullStateChanged:
    m_PersistentCalls:
      m_Calls: []
  m_text: "'Summer 1947'\n\nI wear my best ie, still a little too big, the sleeves
    dancing around my arms. The embroidery is red like the raspberries by the roadside.
    At neighbur Elena's house the musicians tune their violins. \nThe smell of cozonac
    and dus hangs in the warm air. My mother kneels before me, smooths my hair, and
    says: 'Astazi ai voie, Iana. Today you're allowed to dance.' The hora begins.
    \nThe whole yard trembles beneath everyone's feet. I slip into the circle, small
    between wide skirts and heavy boots. Someone takes my hand. I don't know who,
    but the grip is warm, not strict. \nThe women laugh when I almost stumble. The
    men shout rythms, children push each other around me. The circle turns, faster
    and faster, and I feel my heart beating all the way into my figertips. For the
    first time, I belong. For the irst time, the village lifts me up as if I'm light
    enough to float with the music. "
  m_isRightToLeft: 0
  m_fontAsset: {fileID: 11400000, guid: e981119c4fb8360468cb3e2f08c2f99f, type: 2}
