  m_Maskable: 1
  m_OnCullStateChanged:
    m_PersistentCalls:
      m_Calls: []
  m_text: "'Summer 1965'\n\nThe air is warm and smells of dust and wild mint. All
    the children are outside. Some jump rope, others roll tires down the hill. \nFrom
    the pond nearby comes the whining of frogs, as if they're joining the game. And
    a boy sits on the curb,. biting into a ripe peach, the juice runs down his chin
    and he laughs at nothing. \nThe women sit on wooden bensches, feet in slippers,
    talking softly about the harvest and the neighbours. \nThe men return slowly
    from the fields, sweaty, tired, but laughing. \nThis is the summer evening of
    our village. The kind of silence that's full of sound ... feet on earth, frogs
    in water, sweet fruit in children's hands. "
  m_isRightToLeft: 0
  m_fontAsset: {fileID: 11400000, guid: e981119c4fb8360468cb3e2f08c2f99f, type: 2}
